    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d523">

                <pb facs="0587" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg475"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Sherrill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The department to-day handed the Argentine and Brazilian charges a draft protocol
                    designed to be jointly proposed by the <pb facs="0588" n="476" xml:id="pg476"/>
                    mediating powers at one of the three capitals for signature by the
                    representatives of Ecuador and Peru at that capital for the purpose of the
                    exchange of expressions of regret and for the further purpose of assuring a
                    tranquil and orderly course to the mediation. 60th chargés d’affaires were
                    requested to submit the draft for their Government’s amendments, suggestions, or
                    approval and for suggestion as to the time and place of proposal. Repeat
                    foregoing to the embassy at Petropolis.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
